<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cristoforo Madruzzo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1512–1578</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cristoforo Madruzzo was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a> from 1539 to 1567, later also bishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brixen">Brixen</a>, and a cardinal from 1542. He was host of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a>, which met in his city between 1545 and 1563, and he acted as an intermediary between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> and the Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>. He also served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a> as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> in 1556 and 1557.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cristoforo-madruzzo.jpg" alt="Cristoforo Madruzzo" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_Cardinal_Cristoforo_Madruzzo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
